dsh-element-ref — upstream notice

This project is a successor implementation of dsh-element-picker
(https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-element-picker, version 0.10.2),
published by sakikoTGW and declared MIT in its package.json.

Upstream came first. Credit for the original idea, the problem framing and the
prior work is theirs. The upstream tarball ships no LICENSE file; its MIT
declaration is honored here by attribution rather than by copying a notice
file that does not exist.

Our implementation is independent. Measured against upstream 0.10.2 with
5-token shingles over the whole runtime JavaScript, textual overlap is about
8% (line-set overlap about 4%), concentrated in statements forced by the DSH
plugin API (registering a prefix route, loopback address checks, JSON response
headers, DSH CSS variables).

A small number of identifier names were inherited from reading the upstream
code early on: BUTTON_ID, RECENT_KEY, RECENT_MAX, installStyles, parsePayload,
NS. They are naming habits, not copied implementations.

Upstream architecture: provider/output protocol tables plus a PowerShell/UIA
native channel (protocols.js, native/os-pick.ps1).
Our architecture: one injected kernel shared by four channels, a four-step
insertion fallback (quote card -> chip -> plain text -> clipboard), and a
six-layer element description model.
